       🔴 THE SENTENCE THIS BLOCK FLAGGED AS NOT MEASURED IS NOW MEASURED, and the answer is yes-with-three-
       consequences. An .editorconfig section keyed on the vendored file's REAL path DOES match it: the tree
       goes 852 -> 757 with the property set on St4i.EdgeCore alone, exactly -95, and CS1591 disappears from
       that file. What was not on record:
         (1) It leaves EIGHT CS1573 in the same file. Option (b) above names CS1591 only, so as written it
             exempts one of the vendored file's two documentation codes, not the file.
         (2) An .editorconfig applies at or below its OWN directory, and that file's real path is outside
             tools/machine-simulator — so the section cannot live in this product's tree at all. It has to
             be planted at the REPOSITORY ROOT, above an unrelated TypeScript/Node application, invisible to
             anyone reading this product.
         (3) 757 is not 116. "Leaves the other 448 asserted" is true and is not "passing": (b) removes the
             95 nobody may fix and leaves 641 warnings that must either be written or be pinned.
       So (b) is still the narrower instrument and it is still an override, and it does not on its own make
       the switch settable. W-1 did not take it. The decision is docs/owner-decisions.md item 12, which
       carries this measurement where an owner will be standing; this file is not that place.

       🔴 AND THE HALF THAT NEEDED NO SWITCH WAS TAKEN INSTEAD — tests/St4i.EdgeCore.Tests/
       DocCommentProseTests.cs. It reads every `///` run in the tree as XML and checks every element NAME
       against a registry, which is one thing the compiler does not do at all (Roslyn passes unknown
       elements through, so `<summry>` deletes a summary in silence). It runs in the gate, on every build,
       for ALL fifteen compilations and for files in none of them. It cannot see a cref; that is why item 12
       exists. Its corpus at 46439925 was 530 files and 3,616 blocks — a MEASUREMENT, not a pin: the only
       scalars any assertion there holds are the two FLOORS in
       TheScanReachesItsCorpus_AndTheVendoredFileTheProjectNames (400 files, 2,500 blocks), which exist so a
       walk that stopped finding the tree fails loudly instead of passing vacuously.

       🔴 IT FOUND SOMETHING ON ITS FIRST RUN, which is the argument for it. One live malformed block in
